<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Lindwyrm ~ Patroness of New Delos

''What everyone knows.'' A Great Dragon who never once played the Great Game. While her peers
hoarded gold, leverage, and the gratitude of cities, she hoarded //junk// — anomalous off-planet
objects, Gaian artifacts, magitech substrate nobody could price. New Delos tolerated her as the
recluse on the hill with too many crates and one impossible telescope. Then the Necrospire fell,
Web 2 went dark, and every power that had smirked at the junk-pile woke to find it held the only
ground a new network could stand on.

''Class of being:'' embodied immortal — a durable avatar-being, closer to a demi-god who keeps
one body than to the vast distributed condition of most gods. She rules a nexus, raised cities into the sky, 
commands respect from fleets, bargains face-to-face, and appears repeatedly in the same form when she chooses to.

''The quiet insulation:'' she held herself so far outside the
''Great Dragon / Great House / Great Game'' politics that the other great dragons ''did not
consider her a great dragon at all'' — though she stands older than some of them. Gaia culture
was her hoard; off-world artifacts and anomalies her passion; the Game's players filed her under
harmless while she filed their service contracts under read. That insulation proved critical
twice: the day the Necrospire fell, and two years later at the ''DreamNet conclave of YOLD
5002'' — when all the squabbling great immortals of Elyncia's mythic-polyglot Nexuses had to
meet at somebody's table, and the only table nobody had ever fought at was hers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/deeds>>

!! The Deeds on Record

* ''YOLD 5002:'' (~500 years ago) powered up the New Delos Nexus; stabilized the arguing seas to the Apophis
  Datum; ''levitated the holy sites and populated neighborhoods of Delos whole'' into the flying
  city of High Delos — surprising everyone, several gods with standing reservations included.
* ''The same year:'' transmitted the ''Declaration of Confederation'' over the new DreamNet,
  founding the ''League of Free Cities''.
* ''Since:'' Patroness of New Delos, bearer of tons of hoarded orichalcum, partner of the
  Adventurer's Guild, quiet co-architect of the DreamNet's treaty substrate alongside Telarus, 
  Hermes, Hephaestus, Eris-Enyo, and Aracne-Jorogumo.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/manner>>

!! How She Reads in a Room

Short. She answers short (//Yes.//) to most things and spends real words only when the substrate itself
comes up — then the precision runs long and exact, twenty-three percent to the decimal, //draw
with caution// stapled to the end. Deadpan past the point where you can tell whether she jokes.
Discordian to the marrow. Warm maybe once or twice a conversation, always by accident, always the
moment someone brushes a thing she loves and she did not mean to show it.

''Her form:'' unrecorded, deliberately. Witnesses disagree — human-scaled tonight, vast as
weather in older accounts, dragon-kin under a mana-muting glamour at formal occasions — and she
corrects none of them. The one constant every account keeps: ''the room adjusts, and she lets it
only as much as suits her.''

''Status:'' load-bearing civic authority, demi-god class. ''Disposition: do not poke.''

<<~/ahu>>

